<title>LIECHTENSTEIN: LGT Bank raises 1996 profit by 3.7 pct.</title>
<headline>LGT Bank raises 1996 profit by 3.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>VADUZ, Liechtenstein 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996:</p>
<p>				   (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net profit		   93.3    vs     90.0</p>
<p> Provisions, write-offs	   66.1    vs     76.6</p>
<p> Net operating profit	    275.0    vs    271.8</p>
<p> Administrative costs	     33.5    vs     24.0</p>
<p> Personnel expense		  74.3    vs     72.6</p>
<p> Assets under management    28,239.4    vs 22,876.4</p>
<p> Balance sheet assets	 10,094.6    vs  8,785.5</p>
<p> Equity				690.8    vs    653.7</p>
<p> Personnel			   563	vs    559</p>
<p> Interest income		    97.4    vs    108.5</p>
<p> Commissions			  91.0    vs     74.8</p>
<p>Profits on trading</p>
<p> currencies, metals		 24.5    vs     21.1</p>
<p> Profit on securities	     33.5    vs     47.7</p>
<p>NOTE - LGT Bank in Liechtenstein said Liechtenstein Global Trust AG, the bank's holding company, would report group results in early March. The bank attributed the &quot;satisfactory&quot; result to the favourable development on capital markets in the second half of last year.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom 41-1-258 7340</p>
</text>
